    "result_text": "Green. \n\nI agreed with the finding and addressed it. The per-day signup count was duplicated verbatim between `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` and `FlagOwnerBulkSignup`, and since both count the identical thing (owners already registered on a given business day), that was real drift risk the codebase explicitly guards against.\n\nFix: extracted a single `BusinessDays.createdOn(OwnerRepository, LocalDate businessDay)` helper \u2014 placed alongside `effectiveRegistrationDate`, which is already described as the \"single source of truth\" for the business day, so the count built on top of it now lives in the same place. Both rules call it and retain only their own threshold and action:\n- `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` \u2014 `>= 100` \u2192 reject (429).\n- `FlagOwnerBulkSignup` \u2014 `> 80` \u2192 set the warning flag.\n\nThe helper's javadoc also documents the \"persisted owners only\" semantic (so a pre-`SaveOwner` caller doesn't count the owner being created), which both callers rely on. Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
